wlroots 0.17.4: tag an X11 present with the commit_seq its commit gets

The X11 backend tags each PresentPixmap (and the no-buffer PresentNotifyMSC) with
wlr_output.commit_seq read inside the commit, before wlr_output_commit_state() has
incremented it. The commit event that wlr_presentation_time records a feedback's
commit_seq from carries the incremented value, and the PresentCompleteNotify of this
present comes back with the serial it was sent with, so a feedback is only answered
by the present of the commit after its own. The headless and Wayland backends use
commit_seq + 1. Shown under Xvfb with a client that commits its next frame only when
the feedback of the one before has arrived: unpatched, its frames were three host
frames apart where the patched backend gives two with a compositor that commits at
every frame event, and one with a compositor that commits only on change. Unpatched,
with a compositor that commits only on change, the client got no feedback for its
second frame and stopped there.
Found on Dosplex running as an X11 client of SteamOS's Gamescope; applies to the
bundled wlroots and to the development build's subproject (compositor/subprojects).

--- a/backend/x11/output.c
+++ b/backend/x11/output.c
@@ -354,7 +354,14 @@
 
 	pixman_region32_clear(&output->exposed);
 
-	uint32_t serial = output->wlr_output.commit_seq;
+	// The serial comes back in PresentCompleteNotify as the commit_seq of the
+	// present event. wlr_output_commit_state() increments commit_seq after this
+	// commit succeeds and the commit event carries the incremented value, which
+	// is what wlr_presentation_time matches a present event against. Tag the
+	// present with the value this commit is about to get, as the headless and
+	// Wayland backends do, so the feedback of a commit completes with its own
+	// present and not with the next one.
+	uint32_t serial = output->wlr_output.commit_seq + 1;
 	uint32_t options = 0;
 	uint64_t target_msc = output->last_msc ? output->last_msc + 1 : 0;
 	xcb_present_pixmap(x11->xcb, output->win, x11_buffer->pixmap, serial,
@@ -403,7 +410,9 @@
 			return false;
 		}
 	} else if (output_pending_enabled(wlr_output, state)) {
-		uint32_t serial = output->wlr_output.commit_seq;
+		// See output_commit_buffer(): the serial is the commit_seq this commit
+		// is about to get.
+		uint32_t serial = output->wlr_output.commit_seq + 1;
 		uint64_t target_msc = output->last_msc ? output->last_msc + 1 : 0;
 		xcb_present_notify_msc(x11->xcb, output->win, serial, target_msc, 0, 0);
 	}
